+   -- System 573 (psx_patches/0027): the SECOND PS1 memory card (joypad_mem #2, ~64 ALM)
+   -- is removed. Only PS1 card 1 is a real 573 use (DDR / Dancing-Stage edit data saves
+   -- to a single card); no 573 game mounts a 2nd card. Card 1 (ijoypad_mem1 above) is
+   -- KEPT. The mem2 master-port outputs are tied idle so the PSX DDR3 memory arbiter
+   -- never sees a card-2 request, and the SIO0 OR-bus contributions are tied benign:
+   --   mem2_request/WE/RD = 0  -> no DDR3 traffic from the absent card
+   --   isActiveMem2       = 0  -> slotIdle for the pad/card1 stays correct
+   --   receiveValidMem2/ackMem2/receiveBufferMem2 = 0 -> OR-bus no-ops
+   isActiveMem2     <= '0';
+   receiveValidMem2 <= '0';
+   receiveBufferMem2 <= (others => '0');
